OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sG"NO NEW EVIDENCE"
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGON BIRMINGHAM SIX
OL,4,D
OL,5, The Home Office has said that a Granada
OL,6, TV programme offered no new evidence on
OL,7, the case of the Birmingham Six.
OL,9,FProgramme makers said they were putting
OL,10,Fforward new information which would
OL,11,Fclear the six convicted men.
OL,13,FBut the Home Office said the programme
OL,14,Finformation had been studied carefully
OL,15,Fand it offered nothing new.
OL,17,FIt said a Special Branch document which
OL,18,Fthe programme used was written after
OL,19,Fthe six's trial and was investigated
OL,20,Fby the police - one result was that a
OL,21,Fman was jailed for 12 years.
OL,23,D]FFromG29-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
