OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGTV FOUR "WERE IRA
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGOFFICERS" - DEAR
OL,4,D
OL,5, Four men named on TV as the Birmingham
OL,6, pub bombers were probably IRA officers
OL,7, in charge of the bombings, says the
OL,8, chief constable of the West Midlands.
OL,10,FBut Geoffrey Dear said the Birmingham
OL,11,FSix - the six men in jail for the 1974
OL,12,Fbombings - were the "soldiers" for the
OL,13,Fattacks in which 21 people died.
OL,15,FMr Dear said the four, who he named,
OL,16,Fwere suspects at the time and one of
OL,17,Fthem was charged, along with the six,
OL,18,Fwith conspiracy to cause explosions.
OL,20,FMr Dear said police knew more men were
OL,21,Finvolved throughout their inquiries.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG29-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
