OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774820541
OL,1,Vk4                               G8/22
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGTHREE CHARGED OVER
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGILLEGAL EXPORTS
OL,4,D
OL,5, Three people have been charged with
OL,6, attempting to smuggle electrical
OL,7, components through Heathrow to Iraq.
OL,9,FToufic Fouad Amyuni, 37, of Fawcett
OL,10,FSt, West Brompton, London and Ali
OL,11,FAshour Daghir, 49, of Drake Close,
OL,12,FEsher, Surrey, were remanded in custody
OL,13,F
OL,14,FUxbridge Magistrates Court released
OL,15,FJeanine Celestine Speckman, 41, of
OL,16,FBates Walk, Addlestone, Surrey, on bail
OL,18,FAn Iraqi man is to be deported after
OL,19,Ftrigger devices capable of detonating
OL,20,Fnuclear bombs were found at Heathrow
OL,21,FAirport yesterday.
OL,23,D]FFromG29-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774820541
OL,1,Vk5     ($             h4        G9/22
OL,2,Vz%s{4~!j5s{4k7}jwj7}j?
OL,3,V  z5 j5z5j5*upj5j5
OL,5, Foreign Secretary Douglas Hurd has
OL,6, rejected breaking off relations with
OL,7, Iraq over the seizure of nuclear
OL,8, weapon triggers at Heathrow.
OL,10,FHe said this would leave two Britons in
OL,11,Fprison in Baghdad without protection
OL,12,Fand Britain with no embassies between
OL,13,Fthe Khyber Pass and the Mediterranean.
OL,15,FMr Hurd said he could seen no advantage
OL,16,Fand considerable risk in breaking off
OL,17,Fdiplomatic relations.
OL,19,FHe conceded, however, the need for
OL,20,FBritain to be vigilant in its dealings
OL,21,Fwith Iraq.
OL,22,D
OL,23,D]FFromG29-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
