OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774820541
OL,1,Vk4                              G12/22
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMANDELA AND BUTHELEZI
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGTO HOLD PEACE TALKS
OL,4,D
OL,5, South Africa's two most powerful black
OL,6, leaders have agreed to meet for peace
OL,7, talks after an upsurge of fierce
OL,8, fighting between anti-apartheid groups.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FNelson Mandela and Mangosuthu Buthelezi
OL,11,Fhave called an unprecedented meeting
OL,12,Ffor next Monday, signalling a peace
OL,13,Fbreakthrough.
OL,15,FClashes between black factions in the
OL,16,Fpast two days have killed at least 18
OL,17,Fpeople and made hundreds homeless.
OL,19,FThey will seek to end the fighting in
OL,20,FNatal between Mr Buthelezi's Inkatha
OL,21,Fgroup and Mr Mandela's ANC.
OL,23,D]FFromG29-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
